  "result": {
    "text": "```python\ndef sum_squares(lst):\n    total = 0\n    for i, num in enumerate(lst, start=1):\n        if (i % 3) == 0:\n            total += num ** 2\n        else if i % 4 == 0:\n            total += num ** 3\n        else:\n            total += num\n    return total\n```\n\nExplanation:\n- The function iteratesates over the elements of the list.\n- It checks the index of the element and both, the index and the actual value of the index.\n- If the the index is a multiple of 3, it squares the element.\n- If the index is a multiple of 4, it cubes the element.\n- If the index is not a multiple of 3 or 4, it adds the element unchanged.\n- Finally, the function returns the sum of all the elements.",
